=== SIGNATURE ===
z_change_costs(du, cap)

=== COMMENT ===
Private helper for make_change - do not call directly. Unbounded-coin DP: returns a column of length cap+1 where row a+1 is the fewest coins that total exactly a units, or 1000000000 (sentinel) if a is not reachable. du is the denominations in integer GCD-units (entries below 1 are ignored).

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(du, cap, LET(
   inf, 1000000000,
   IF(cap < 1,
      0,
      LET(
         alen, cap + 1,
         init, VSTACK(0, SEQUENCE(cap, 1, inf, 0)),
         REDUCE(init, SEQUENCE(cap), LAMBDA(best, pass_num,
            REDUCE(best, du, LAMBDA(acc, coin,
               IF(coin < 1,
                  acc,
                  LET(
                     shifted, TAKE(VSTACK(SEQUENCE(coin, 1, inf, 0), best), alen),
                     IF(shifted + 1 < acc, shifted + 1, acc)
                  )
               )
            ))
         ))
      )
   )
))

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Private helper for make_change. Builds the minimum-coins-per-amount table by dynamic programming.

Arguments:
  du  - the coin denominations expressed as positive integers (in GCD units); entries below 1 are ignored as unusable.
  cap - the largest amount (in the same units) to solve for.

Returns:
  A column of cap+1 values. Row a+1 holds the fewest coins whose values sum to exactly a units, or 1000000000 if a cannot be made. When cap < 1 it returns the scalar 0 (only amount 0, which needs 0 coins).

Implementation note: this is a shift-based Bellman-Ford relaxation - each pass, every coin shifts the whole best vector down by its size (VSTACK a column of sentinels on top, then TAKE back to length cap+1) and takes the element-wise min of best and shifted+1. cap passes guarantee convergence (a solution never needs more than cap coins). It deliberately avoids INDEX-ing into the growing accumulator with a computed index: Excel returns wrong results for that pattern when the inputs trace back to a range or when several make_change calls share a sheet.

Called only by make_change; not intended for direct worksheet use.
